Z||000000||jerpro||03-18-2001||12:06 PM||||For me it would be people over 70 riding those huge cars down the road. A lot of them do not have the skills (anymore) to handle a vehicle. And they are an accident waiting to happen.<BR>I think they should make mandatory testing for people over 70 to requalify for a drivers licence.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tina||03-18-2001||12:44 PM||||Agreed, but cellphones take the cake.<BR>Makes me wanna rig up something like'<BR>a flashing display.<P>"OFF WITH IT,OR FIND SOMEWHERE TO PARK"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake||03-18-2001||01:07 PM||||ah yes, I've had my run-in with a few of them old folks (literally)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> one time a 77 year old man in a big ole boat actually pulled out of a parking lot and right into the side of my fiero while i was cruisin 35mph down the street. heard of people pulling out in front of ya, but into the side of ya? then he tried to blame it on me when he was talkin to the cop. Yeah, okay! The cop thought he was a nutcase  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> afterwards I sat and smoked a cigarette with the cop while he showed me all his nifty gadgets in his car. <P>what really bugs me is when those "senior" drivers are in front of you with one foot on the brake and the other one on the gas. I can never tell what the hell they're doing, speeding up? slowin down? who knows. I'm just tired of seeing cars accelerate with their brake lights on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>----------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Rxbw.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||03-18-2001||01:39 PM||||Ok lets see, car in front of you is drifting from lane to lane. When opportunity presents itself you pass and toot your horn. You startle the jerk out of his stupor and he makes and obscene gesture. You accelerate past and he gives chase, now what? I would like to pull over and climb my 6.2 230 frame out of my little sports car, but my wife doesn’t approve of my road rage. At least he is watching the road now. I really can’t stand those drivers talking on the phone.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||03-18-2001||01:47 PM||||there was this guy when i was coming down here to NC...i was doing about 75 in the Fiero in the fastlane. guy up ahead of me, i get up close to him, ya know since he is doing about 55... after a couple seconds of me right behind him, i flash my lights once, in case he didnt see me...nothing. flashed a few more times (he's still going 55 in a 65) finally the trucker who was right next to him (why i couldnt pass in slow lane) moved over...as soon as i had a free lane, the @sshole sped up. i passed him and continued on my way. im doing like 80 at this point, so i could get a bit ahead of him, and in his little dae woo he gets on my ass and starts flashing his brights. too bad my wing blocked them so it didnt bother me at all. why do some people just want to be jerk offs?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||03-18-2001||02:09 PM||||i already mentioned one of mine in another post. just got back from germany lisa, and that definitly wouldn't have happened there. they take keeping the fast lane clear seriouly. america will never be able to to have speed limits like that because of the drivers themselves. <P>the funniest old people story experience i know of was coming across someone i knew trying to get out a parking spot. some old woman had parked so crooked she couldn't get her car out. she had her kid watching one side and this old woman watching the other. this old woman is telling the kid "your mother didn't park strait".||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||03-18-2001||02:26 PM||||I've had a few encounters with old people too.. there's this one lady in my town, she's under 5 feet tall, and can barely see over her steering wheel.. last summer I was driving home, abouty a block from my house, and she was driving right down the middle of the street... I had to swerve into the entrance of a parking lot to avoid her, and she didn't even slow down... then, a couple of weeks later, the same old lady went right through a stop sign. I had to hit the brakes otherwise she would have smashed my fender.. at the time I thought maybe I should have, cause it would have been her fault, and we would have gotten the car fixed for free and she would likely get her license taken away.. but I just complained about it for a few days then everyone forgot.<P>People talking on cell phones while driving are pretty bad too, over spring break someone turned a corner and turned into the wrong lane.... luckily I was slowing down for the stop sign anyway, so I was able to get out of the way (I brushed a snowbank though, but missed the other car) I don't even think the person saw me...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000007||TheFiero64||03-18-2001||02:53 PM||||The thing that pisses me off the most is the A%%holes that don't  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <B>USE THERE BLINKERS</B>!<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||8
Z||000008||TwisT||03-18-2001||03:07 PM||||Don't you know???  Some of them' there cars came with that turn-signal delete option from the factory!  LOL...<P>I hate tail-gater's myself.  They get RIGHT on your ass (usually driving some sort of huge pickup or SUV).  I usually have enough curtousy to speed up,  but even then they just can't seem to stop cutting their toe-nails in the fan blades.<P>Luckily the Fiero is quick and nimble,  much like a sport-bike,  which is good to get away from situations...<P>Brett ||||reg||1
Z||000009||hugh||03-18-2001||03:14 PM||||How about when you pull behind someone at a signal light and when it turns green they move up 2 feet and put on their left turn signal.||||reg||1
Z||000010||007DOUG||03-18-2001||03:26 PM||||People that don't understand what an entrance lane is for. Step on the damn gas and merge. DON'T stop at the end of the ramp and wait for traffic!!!!!!<P>Whats a tail-gater? Never seen one of those  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>86 SE V6 153K (daily)<BR>86 GT red <BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT w/4:10 tranny<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>88 Coupe<BR>88 Formula 5 speed (soon)<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>But......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||13
Z||000011||Cheever2||03-18-2001||03:35 PM||||I'll add my vote to the that of not using the signals to turn or change lanes.  If someone tries to get into my lane in front of me without signaling, I do everything I can to prevent it.  But if they only have the common courtesy to signal, which is like ASKING if they can move over, then I allow it every time.  All they have to do is ask.<P>Lisa, I think most people don't understand the concept of a "fast lane", or why slower cars should stay to the right.  Those people can never play simple board games (let alone chess), because they do not even see the consequences of their next move.<P>Everybody be careful on their trips to Daytona.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000012||TigerFiero||03-18-2001||04:05 PM||||I am with Fiero64.  For those who can not take the split second it takes to hit the blinker, they are the bigest #@%*$ on the road.  My road rage goes into overtime if you pull in front of me and don't use your blinker.  Makes me wish I drove a big rig so I could just hit them and say "I don't know what happened, he just pulled right in front of me."<P>------------------<BR>TigerFiero<BR>86 Sport Coupe<BR>86 GT Fastback<BR>North Florida/South Georgia Fieros||||reg||8
Z||000013||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-18-2001||04:16 PM||||drive below the speed limit in the fast lane<BR>pull out without looking<BR>turn right without stopping first<BR>run red lights<BR>stop at the end of a merge ramp<BR>go slow, then accelerate when you try to pass, then go slow once you are stuck behind them again<BR>stop so far back from the left turn light that the light won't "trip"<P>Most Serious/Biggest Complaint:  Try to run me off the road, or grab me as I pass by on my motorcycle.  If anybody every succeeds at this, I WILL PRESS CHARGES FOR ATTEMPTED MURDER OR MY WIFE WILL IF IT IS A SUCCESSFUL MURDER ATTEMPT.  If you see someone do this, warn them they are facing long term incarceration if they kill someone.  And, they will probably loose a limb in the case of reaching out to grab a motorcycle!<P>Can you beleive how stupid some people are out there????  <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Black88GT||03-18-2001||04:20 PM||||The blinker thing I can live with (unless they slam on the brakes and turn violently).  It depends on when you ask me this question because I run into so many of the things mentioned already on a daily basis thats its tough to put my finger on the worst.  <P>With that being said, I hate when people <B>RUBBERNECK!</B>  You know, when they slow down on the highway to like 30 mph just because a cop pulled someone over or an accident happened, or even if someone is changing a tire.  I mean, what the hell is so fascinating about a cop giving someone a ticket?  Is it really worth causing a back up and making me and a bunch of others late to work?  That really gets me.  FieroLisa brought up another one, had that happen to me before.  Like 007Doug said, the merging thing is a problem too.  Some people just don't understand how to merge with traffic, they just slam on the brakes and sit there.  Like I said these happen to me on a daily basis since I use the highway everyday (fun to be me).<P>About the old people thing.  I don't understand why there is such an emphasis on younger drivers and not really old ones.  My theory has been this.  A) under 18 drivers can't vote therefore they have no say B) Younger drivers drive every day to school or work or wherever, much more then the average senior citizen who drives their Caprice classic to the supermarket once a week. <P>I like when people try to speed up when I pass them.  I just laugh, downshift, and floor it to make them look stupid.  Usually they are driving some big sedan or an SUV that has no chance.<P>just my 2 cents<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||88formula||03-18-2001||07:27 PM||||Usually I don't let that stuff bother me anymore. Getting angry about it is too much work and accomplishes nothing.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||rogergarrison||03-18-2001||08:05 PM||||1. hate SUVs that tailgate<BR>2. hate SUVs going 90mph<BR>3. hate  people entering from on ramps without looking<P>   I give lots of brake checks to idiots, if they lose control n spin out tough luck.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||KnightRyder31||03-18-2001||08:10 PM||||When people drive BELOW the speed limit!<BR>When people ride your @ss and flash their brights at you!<BR>When people pass you for no reason and cut you off!<BR>When people try to race you, and when they lose, they flick you off, or point a gun at you!!!!<BR>When people pull on to the road, right in front of you!<BR>When people slam on there breaks for no reason!<P>I'm sorry, I guess I'm just an angry person!||||reg||1
Z||000018||87GT||03-18-2001||08:18 PM||||I hate it when Im crusing along at about 5 mph over the limit, then some jerk runs right up on my ass and tries to get me to speed it up.  I usually slow down on curves because I know it irritates the hell out of the driver on my rear.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
