Z||000056||Tigger||03-26-2001||01:00 PM||||I rarely use a turn signal when no one is around, It's almost like you're talking to yourself.<P>Ok this happened awhile ago, two lane road, pull up to a stop sign, a woman pulls up next to me in the right hand turn lane, I expect she's going to turn right.  Wrong!  I'm making my way through the intersection and "what the...."  I have to slam on the brakes as she's cutting me off getting back into my lane.  If she made a mistake or just plain didn't know where she was going, she could have at least let me go, then follow.  But No!  I made sure I let her know my appreciation for almost running into me by following her "real" close for the next mile.  Probably wasn't the smartest thing to do, but I can bet she'll think before doing something stupid like that again.<P>Disclaimer:  I have nothing against women drivers in general, this one just ticked me off that day.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
